35,2,1,talk,Rin,,"Wow, I found some things! The bin house at the station block smells really sour in the summer—even worse than our pile! And the next lane has people watching the trash for fifty minutes. That's a long time!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Midori,,"That sounds quite exhausting for the neighbors! As for the costs, I found that we've been spending about thirty-four thousand yen annually on maintenance, and new shelters can be quite expensive, even with a forty percent subsidy.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"It seems the ""burden"" is quite concentrated. Most complaints come from the house right next to the bins. Also, the truck arrives quite early, which explains why some of us are caught off guard.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,"Well, it looks like the ""dream"" setup is a nightmare! The station block spent two years bickering over a broken latch and sweeping duties. And the paperwork for a permanent build? Four months and a site plan! Talk about a headache.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The physical constraints are significant; one frontage is barely ninety centimeters wide, while others are much larger. Furthermore, the residents' meeting revealed a complete lack of willingness to enforce rules regarding late bags.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Rin,,"Wait, so a bin house is actually a stinky trap? That's scary! And standing there for fifty minutes sounds like a super long time to just watch trash. I don't think either of those are very fun!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Midori,,"It really does sound like a lot of work for the neighbors. Since we're already spending over thirty thousand yen a year just on maintenance, maybe we can find a way to reduce those costs while keeping things clean.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"Exactly. And since one neighbor is doing most of the complaining, it's clear the current spot is a point of resentment. If we don't address that specific friction, no amount of budget-cutting will fix the mood.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"Exactly! And let's not forget the ""hidden"" cost of our sanity. If the station block is still fighting over a latch, imagine us trying to manage a permanent build with all that paperwork. It sounds like a total trap.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"If the current spot is a source of resentment, it is likely because the burden is not shared. We cannot ignore that some frontages are far too narrow to host the point without causing significant hardship.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Rin,,"If the bin house is stinky and watching trash is boring, maybe we should think of something totally different! I don't want us to fight over latches like the other block. What else can we do?","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Midori,,"Maybe we could look for a simpler solution that doesn't require expensive construction or constant supervision. If we can lower the annual maintenance costs, it would be much easier for everyone to agree.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,Let's be realistic. We have a neighbor who's fed up and a truck that arrives before half of us are awake. Moving the point or changing the schedule is the only way to stop the bleeding.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"Moving it sounds like a plan, but let's be careful. If we just ""agree"" to a new spot without a strict schedule, the same person will end up doing all the work. I'm not interested in a new kind of headache!","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Asuka,,May is correct. A simple agreement to move the point is insufficient. We must establish a rotation or a shared responsibility system that accounts for the varying widths of our frontages to ensure no one is unfairly burdened.,"{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Rin,,"I don't want anyone to be sad or grumpy! If we move it, let's make sure it's a place where everyone feels happy. Can we find a way that isn't stinky or boring?","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Midori,,"I agree, Rin. Let's aim for a solution that's gentle on everyone. If we can find a spot that's fair and a cost that doesn't strain any household's budget, I think we'll all be much happier.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"Gentle is fine, Midori, but fairness is what stops the fighting. We have a clear hotspot of resentment and a logistical timing issue. Let's focus on a solution that actually relieves the person currently suffering.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,"Let's be real: ""fairness"" usually means the person who says yes first does everything. I want a plan where the actual hours of work are mapped out, not just a vague promise to be ""gentle."" No more invisible labor!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"Precisely. We must avoid a situation where the burden remains static. Given the frontage measurements, we cannot simply rotate the location randomly; we need a structured plan that acknowledges the physical limitations of each property.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
