60,3,1,talk,Rin,,I don't like Option A because watching trash for fifty minutes is way too boring! And Option C is a stinky trap! I think Option B is the best because it's like a little adventure for the trash!,"{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Midori,,"I'm a bit worried about Option C because the construction costs are quite high, even with the subsidy. Option B sounds interesting, but I wonder if moving the point frequently would be too much trouble for everyone.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,Option A is a recipe for more fighting; we've already seen that people hate supervising. Option C is a bureaucratic nightmare. Option B is the only one that actually relieves the person currently bearing the brunt of the complaints.,"{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,May,,"Option C is a total non-starter with that paperwork, and A is just a fancy way of saying ""stand around and be bored."" B is the only one that actually shifts the burden. Let's go with B!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Option B is the most logical choice to ensure equity, but it must be implemented with a strict schedule. We cannot ignore that some frontages are too narrow; the rotation must be adjusted to accommodate those physical constraints.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Rin,,"Yay! Everyone seems to like Option B! As long as we don't have to stand around and watch the trash, I'm happy. Let's make it a fun rotation so nobody gets grumpy!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Midori,,"If everyone is in agreement, I'm happy too. As long as we can manage the rotation without it becoming a financial or physical burden for any one household, it seems like a very fair compromise.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"Let's not get carried away with ""fun."" The goal here is to stop the resentment. If we rotate the location, the person who's been complaining for three years finally gets a break, and we all learn to coexist.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,May,,"Exactly! As long as the rotation is written in stone and not just a ""suggestion,"" it'll actually work. I'm voting for B, provided we don't let the ""first person to answer the phone"" handle the logistics!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"I will also vote for Option B. However, we must explicitly document that the rotation period for the narrowest frontage is reduced or modified, ensuring that no one is forced to compromise their access.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Rin,,I'm voting for Option B! It's the only one that isn't boring or stinky. Let's make it a rule that we all help each other so everyone stays smiling!,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Midori,,"I'll vote for Option B as well. It avoids the high costs of construction and the stress of supervision. If we support each other during the rotation, I'm sure we can maintain a wonderful harmony.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,I'm voting for Option B. It's the only rational way to dissolve the current tension and ensure we can actually look each other in the eye without thinking about trash. Let's just get it done.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,May,,I'm voting for Option B! It's the only way to stop the invisible labor from piling up on one person. Let's just make sure the schedule is ironclad so nobody gets played!,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"I vote for Option B. It is the only viable path to true equity, provided we formally acknowledge the physical limitations of each frontage to prevent any single household from being unfairly disadvantaged.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Rin,,I'm so glad we all agree! Option B is the winner! Now we can all walk past the corner and be happy together. Yay for the trash adventure!,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Midori,,"It really is a relief that we've found a solution we all agree on. I'm sure that by being considerate of each other's situations, we can make this work beautifully. I'm looking forward to our new start!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,"Finally. As long as we actually stick to the rotation and stop the bickering, we might actually survive as neighbors. Let's just hope the ""adventure"" doesn't lead to a new set of complaints.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over.""}]}"
78,3,4,pass,Shunichi,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
79,3,4,talk,May,,"I'm just glad we're not spending four months on paperwork or standing around like statues. Let's get that schedule written down before anyone ""volunteers"" to do it all!","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over.""}]}"
80,3,4,pass,May,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
81,3,4,talk,Asuka,,"The consensus is clear. I will support the implementation of Option B, provided the final agreement explicitly accounts for the frontage measurements to ensure the burden is distributed logically and fairly.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
